  "body": "What changed:\n- The shared `auto_value` widget (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/form.rs`) read Auto from `value == 0`.\n- Typing \"0\", \"0.\" or \"0.5\" passes through 0. The toggle then flipped back to Auto and the typed text was lost.\n- The widget now keeps the manual state while the edit field has focus. When focus leaves with 0, the field reads Auto, as before.\n- `auto_opt` is not affected: `Some(0.0)` is not `None`.\n\nParameters covered (all use `auto_value`):\n- Lead page: Descent helix pitch, Max stay-down distance.\n- Approach page: Ramp angle, Max ramp leg, Minimum radius, Helix pitch, Helix angle, Arc radius, Arc sweep, Ramp / helix / arc feed, Entry plunge feed.\n- Boundary: Extend past open edges.\n- Holes page: Peck depth.\n- Turning page: Bar advance, Probe budget.\n\nPinned by: `egui_app::tests::auto_input_manual::typing_over_an_auto_off_input_keeps_it_manual`. It fails before the fix at the key \"0\". It types 0, \".\", 5 over several frames on Helix pitch and asserts that Auto stays off. It then applies the draft and checks the live value is 0.5. One undo restores Auto (0).\n\nTests run: `camcraft-ui` lib, 933 pass, 1 fail (`stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`, known #2170, fix in PR #2171). Clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-ui` is clean. `cargo xtask gate quick` ran geometry and kernel suites and hit the time limit, so it did not finish.\n\nNot exercised:\n- Only Helix pitch is typed in a test. The other parameters share the widget but have no own test.\n- Save and reopen, and MCP, are not tested. A manual value is a non-zero number in the operation parameters, so both carry it as before.\n- A typed 0 that stays focused is held as manual in the UI. The draft stores 0, which the generator reads as Auto. It does not change posted output of a saved project.\n- Dragging a value to 0 still reads as Auto.\n\nChangelog: Fixed: an Auto input on the operation page no longer switches back to Auto while you type a value.\nEffort: medium\nFixes #2178\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
